WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.017 --> 00:00:03.397
- "Nutritionists Reveal
Humans With Proper Diet

00:00:03.397 --> 00:00:04.907
"Should Not Be Defecating."

00:00:04.907 --> 00:00:05.870
(laughs)
What?

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.150
I know we're facing scary times right now

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:10.040
but I thought it's time for us

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.000
to let it loose for a little bit

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.220
and have a little fun.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.320
And instead of reacting
to our usual memes,

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.760
I decided to react to some

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.220
of the headlines and
articles from The Onion.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.160
For those of you who don't know,

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.600
The Onion is a satirical newspaper,

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.650
none of their headlines
or articles are true.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:25.960
So I hope to get a good laugh,

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.570
don't get offended, it's comedy,

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:28.690
we're here to have a good time.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:29.537
You ready?
Beep!

00:00:29.537 --> 00:00:32.847
"Excited Patient Points Out Organ He Wants

00:00:32.847 --> 00:00:36.550
"From Kidney Tank In Hospital Lobby."

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.740
I don't need to read the article (laughs)

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.477
look at the little kidney floating.

00:00:40.477 --> 00:00:42.077
"Badass Surgeon Puts On

00:00:42.077 --> 00:00:45.670
"Fingerless Latex Gloves
Before Operating."

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:48.830
The dirtiest, meaning the most infectious

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.440
full of bacteria and viruses

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.727
part of your hand are the fingertips.

00:00:53.727 --> 00:00:57.640
"Dr. Scholl's Introduces New
Freeze-Away Toe Remover."

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:58.670
Oh, I have this thing.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.963
I've actually used it
'cause I had a, wait.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:04.723
It got me.

00:01:04.723 --> 00:01:07.160
Chicago foot-care brand
Dr. Scholl's unveiled its

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.400
Freeze-Away Toe Remover Thursday,

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.960
an over-the-counter treatment
that combines freeze therapy

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.010
with fast-acting liquid to loosen

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.450
and ultimately expel unsightly toes.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:17.283
Not gonna lie,

00:01:17.283 --> 00:01:19.710
my toes are looking rather
rough during this pandemic.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.070
The struggle is real.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:22.230
I'm self-pedicuring.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.820
I'm not good at it.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.020
The real product that The Onion is doing

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:28.160
a witty satire of is actually

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.680
a freeze away treatment for plantar warts.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.250
If this specific treatment thingy

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.380
doesn't work for you at home,

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:37.500
we have one where we do this
cryotherapy in our offices.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.020
I wonder if anyone like clicked on this

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:41.767
and they're like ooh, that
toe was getting in the way.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:45.087
"Health Insurance CEO Reveals
Key To Company's Success

00:01:45.087 --> 00:01:48.610
"Is Not Paying For
Customers' Medical Care."

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.480
Just the other day I had a patient,

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.270
I prescribed them a medicine
for a common antibiotic,

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:54.660
send it into the pharmacy,

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.190
pharmacy says insurance not paying for it.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.210
I'm like what, it's like one
of the most common antibiotics.

00:01:58.210 --> 00:01:59.043
Get on the phone,

00:01:59.043 --> 00:02:00.980
spend half an hour arguing
with the insurance company

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:02.090
and what did they tell me?

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:04.580
Oh it's 'cause you ordered
capsule version not the tablets.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:07.580
If you'd just order the tablets
it would have been fine.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:09.857
You owe me half hour of my life back.

00:02:09.857 --> 00:02:11.886
"Tips For Finding The Right Doctor."

00:02:11.886 --> 00:02:13.320
(laughs)

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.980
Just by the photo, I'm
already excited for this tip.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.940
Ask yourself what your personal goals are

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:18.980
when you see a doctor.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:21.620
Do you want to live, or die?

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.720
Do you want to prevent
illnesses, or contract them?

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.920
The goal is to live
and the goal is to have

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.570
the least amount of illness possible.

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:30.750
Doctors can provide better
care when they treat

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.610
your whole family, so try to get

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.170
the same primary care physician

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.674
for your spouse, children, and pets.

00:02:36.674 --> 00:02:38.820
(laughs) I was gonna
say this is a good one

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.160
and then they threw in pets.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.390
A skilled physician
should be able to detect

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.940
any potential health problems,

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:48.520
so never tip them off by
revealing any of your symptoms.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.353
No!

00:02:49.353 --> 00:02:50.186
We need your help.

00:02:50.186 --> 00:02:54.540
The history is probably the
most important part of the exam

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.590
with the physical being
the second most important.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.760
I guess it depends on the
illness I'm trying to diagnose.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:02:59.820
Ask them straight up

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.080
if they've ever killed
a patient on purpose.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.240
Hey Doc, you ever did that to a patient?

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.800
Tell your doctor your fidney hurts.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.086
A good one will know that
that's not real organ.

00:03:10.086 --> 00:03:10.919
(laughs)

00:03:10.919 --> 00:03:12.920
A good one will know what you mean.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:16.610
No, no, no, a good one will know to ask

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:19.150
what you meant without
sounding judgmental.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:21.150
Other patients can be your best allies

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.930
when it comes to finding the right doctor.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:23.763
Agreed.

00:03:23.763 --> 00:03:25.260
Ask friends and coworkers
if you can sit in

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.160
on their physical to get a feel

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.550
for what their doctor's like.

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:29.644
HIPAA.
(siren buzzing)

00:03:29.644 --> 00:03:30.477
HIPAA.

00:03:30.477 --> 00:03:31.430
Make sure they have kind eyes

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.460
that crinkle at the
corners when they smile.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.130
Aw, does your doctor have crow's feet?

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.110
That means they care.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:39.470
Many health care professionals
are increasingly rigid

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:41.500
when it comes to prescribing medications.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:45.030
Remind your doctor that with a
couple of bad online reviews,

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.240
you can bring it all crumbling down.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.560
Man this is so true.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.720
People that run their own businesses,

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.870
they're between a rock and a hard place.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:55.630
If a patient comes in
requesting a specific treatment

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.880
or a specific test and
the doctor doesn't think

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.180
it's in the patient's best interest

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:01.230
but the patient threatens
them with a bad review,

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:02.170
what are you left to do?

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:03.470
And you know what the worst part is?

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:06.760
Let's say the patient leaves
a fraudulent negative review,

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.740
says the doctor did so and so

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.230
and the doctor knows it's untrue,

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:13.265
they can't go on and say
that because of HIPPA.

00:04:13.265 --> 00:04:14.098
(alarm buzzes)

00:04:14.098 --> 00:04:14.931
Patient privacy.

00:04:14.931 --> 00:04:16.590
Above all, don't put to
much pressure on yourself,

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.639
you'll meet the right
doctor when you're ready.

00:04:18.639 --> 00:04:19.472
(laughs)

00:04:19.472 --> 00:04:20.305
It sounds like a dating line.

00:04:20.305 --> 00:04:22.030
No, in all seriousness
it's really important

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.300
to find the right doctor
because if you have a healthy

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.690
doctor-patient relationship,

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:27.770
you're more likely to have
better health outcomes.

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:29.330
And if the first one isn't right,

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.677
always look for a second opinion.

00:04:30.677 --> 00:04:33.637
"I'm In Witness
Protection- I Mean, Doctor,

00:04:33.637 --> 00:04:36.687
"I Work At Doctor,' Says New Neighbor."

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:38.423
What?

00:04:38.423 --> 00:04:41.853
"I'm In Witness
Protection- I Mean, Doctor,

00:04:42.697 --> 00:04:45.687
"I Work At Doctor,' Says New Neighbor."

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:50.943
Anybody?

00:04:50.943 --> 00:04:52.450
- [Narrator] 12 seconds later.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:53.450
- [Crewman] So he's covering up--

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:54.773
- Oh, got it, okay.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:57.950
- [Crewman] That was just (mumbles).

00:04:57.950 --> 00:04:58.783
- I need to do better.

00:04:58.783 --> 00:05:01.613
"Grandfathers Accidentally
Switched at Hospital".

00:05:01.613 --> 00:05:03.270
(laughs)

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:05.980
In yet another disturbing
case of hospital negligence,

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:08.330
two elderly grandfathers
were accidentally switched

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:11.250
at the Cedar-Mount Sinai
Medical Center in Los Angeles

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.850
and sent home with the wrong families.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:14.850
I think this is poking
fun at the fact that

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:17.420
back in the day people may have
taken the wrong babies home.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.130
But nowadays, we have a
lot of security around

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.450
taking the right baby home.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:26.230
Moms and dads get security
bracelets that if the baby's

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:27.860
approaching one of the exit doors

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.460
they won't open unless
the father or mother

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.810
have also their security bracelets on.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.320
So no one's taking the wrong baby home,

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:35.460
nor are they stealing one.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.707
But the elderly, that's funny.

00:05:36.707 --> 00:05:39.427
"Russell Westbrook Quietly
Asks Rockets Team Doctor

00:05:39.427 --> 00:05:42.190
"If He Needs To Make Free
Throw To Pass Physical."

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.023
Why?

00:05:43.023 --> 00:05:44.140
Is he so bad at free throws?

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:45.373
He's like 70%.

00:05:45.373 --> 00:05:46.206
- [Crewman] 62.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:48.173
- That's pretty bad.

00:05:48.173 --> 00:05:51.457
"Nutritionists Reveal
Humans With Proper Diet

00:05:51.457 --> 00:05:53.333
"Should Not Be Defecating."

00:05:53.333 --> 00:05:54.166
(laughs)
What?

00:05:54.166 --> 00:05:55.070
Pooping is great.

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:56.740
Urinating, great.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.140
Are there unhealthy poops?

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:58.973
Yes.

00:05:58.973 --> 00:06:01.450
Are there unhealthy urines, urinations?

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:03.900
Yes, but that's a
question for your doctor.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.300
You know what I'm worried about?

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.680
An article like this gaining traction

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.030
on like an Alex Jones podcast

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:11.446
and then people being like

00:06:11.446 --> 00:06:15.230
oh man, and here I have been for 45 years

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:16.670
pooping my whole life.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:17.797
What have I been eating?

00:06:17.797 --> 00:06:20.327
"Doctor Asks Patient If He Would Mind

00:06:20.327 --> 00:06:21.597
"Having Medical Student,

00:06:21.597 --> 00:06:25.132
"Some Of His Poker
Buddies In Room For Exam."

00:06:25.132 --> 00:06:26.430
(laughs)

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:27.830
If you've never had this happen to you,

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.730
before I bring in a medical student

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:31.850
or a resident with me when I see a patient

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.140
I always ask for permission,
it's the right thing to do,

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:34.973
it's the polite thing to do

00:06:34.973 --> 00:06:36.560
and actually I think
there's rules for it now.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.620
How funny would it be
if your doctor walks in

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:39.670
and is like can I have a medical student?

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:40.503
And you're like sure.

00:06:40.503 --> 00:06:41.970
And you're like, what
about some poker buddies?

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:44.320
And the people that they put
in, the guy with the glasses.

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:46.420
So I used to play poker
semi-professionally

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.770
back in the day when there
was Full Tilt, Ultimate Bet,

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:51.350
Absolute Poker, Poker
Stars, all those good times.

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:53.710
I don't understand why people,
when they play live poker,

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:55.780
they wear dark, reflective glasses.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:58.477
It's like they want
you to see their cards.

00:06:58.477 --> 00:07:02.900
"U.S. Dentists Can't Make
Nation's Teeth Any Damn Whiter."

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.510
You know there's like something
that happens internationally

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.340
where they actually make fun of Americans

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:10.320
for having too white teeth.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.750
They actually make it a joke to say

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.470
oh you Americans with your white teeth.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:15.030
I do think that we do go overboard

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.720
when people do veneers and stuff,

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.950
they bleach their teeth
white like porcelain.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.320
But sometimes it's too white,

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:21.620
like it looks artificial.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.870
I will say that if you
over bleach your teeth,

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:26.480
it will make your teeth
sensitive and it will hurt

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:27.820
so please be careful.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:29.200
This has happened to my friends,

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.800
it's happened to myself
when I was younger,

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.657
made the mistake, not happening again.

00:07:32.657 --> 00:07:35.257
"Exhausted Doctor To Wake Up Early,

00:07:35.257 --> 00:07:37.230
"Finish Surgery in Morning."

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.110
Just moments after successfully stopping

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:41.320
his patient's heart at 10:30 p.m. Tuesday,

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:43.330
bleary-eyed surgeon Dr. Dennis Kelly

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.340
called it a night and
decided to finish performing

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:46.880
quadruple by pass surgery

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:48.847
on Harold Cruz, 67, in the morning.

00:07:48.847 --> 00:07:50.210
"Honestly, all these organs

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:52.290
are looking the same to
me right now," said Kelly.

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:53.840
This is actually a legit struggle.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:57.840
Some surgeries go on for hours.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.490
Pretty much the entire day.

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:02.570
That is why we have teams of surgeons

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:06.640
and surgical residents that
help out in specific operations.

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:07.730
In addition to that,

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:10.430
we always have a backup surgeon on call

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:13.947
in case the surgeon starts
feeling unwell, gets sleepy.

00:08:13.947 --> 00:08:17.377
"ER Doctor Excitedly
Tells Wife He Got To Use

00:08:17.377 --> 00:08:19.057
"Shock Paddle Thing Today."

00:08:19.057 --> 00:08:19.890
(laughs)

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.357
I love the picture of the doctor.

00:08:21.357 --> 00:08:22.867
"I've been wanting to
play with those thingies

00:08:22.867 --> 00:08:24.937
"since my first day, and I finally got to!

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:27.357
"I put them on the guy's
chest, yelled 'Clear!'

00:08:27.357 --> 00:08:29.510
"and they went bzzz just
like they do on TV!"

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:30.510
It's called a defibrillator.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.240
We have to start the segment this way.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.670
Chest compressions, chest
compressions, chest compressions.

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:36.940
You don't run for the
defibrillator until you start

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:38.140
doing chest compressions first,

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:39.550
after of course you call for help.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:40.383
But you can call for help

00:08:40.383 --> 00:08:41.610
while you're doing chest compressions.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:42.990
The reason we do chest compressions

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:45.210
is 'cause you need to buy
time for the defibrillator

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:47.630
to get there, to turn it on,
to make sure it's working,

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:48.463
all that good stuff.

00:08:48.463 --> 00:08:51.290
"Health Scare Prompts Man To
Start Overeating Healthier."

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:52.123
(laughs)

00:08:52.123 --> 00:08:53.290
I love that as it sounds.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:55.030
That's a giant plate of food.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:56.890
It looks healthy, but there's a lot of it.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.440
This has been a real wake-up call for me,

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.870
so from now on, I'm sticking
to eating only nutritious,

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.983
low-fat foods well past
the point of being full.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:07.240
It's not how it works.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:08.240
If you enjoyed this video,

